    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, that's getting a bit weird. \"a rusted Abraham\"? And the bit about the sky screaming until it turned to glass is a little repetitive. It feels like you're just adding more adjectives and \"lore-sounding\" phrases to make it longer rather than actually building new ideas.\n\nActually, checking the dashboard again... the depth_score still hasn't hit the threshold for a Major Quest. It's still hovering way too low. I know I keep saying not to pad it, but the system is really rejecting stuff this short. \n\nCan you try one more time? Try to really flesh out the actual mechanics of the Void-Glass. What were the precursors? Why does the ground pulse like that? Make it long enough to actually feel like a substantial piece of dialogue that the engine will accept. Just... please try to keep the writing tight and not just loop the same imagery. I need actual substance, not just more words.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
